# Git commits

Use Conventional Commits. Keep the subject short. Do not add `Signed-off-by`.

Format: `<type>(optional-scope): <summary>`

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `chore`.

- Imperative summary (`add`, `fix`, `skip`), not past tense
- About 50 characters; add a body only when the why is not obvious
- No `--signoff`, no `Signed-off-by` trailer
- No `--no-verify` unless the user asks
- Pass the message through a HEREDOC
- Commit only when the user asks

```text
feat(chain): share skip and back across CH and rampage
fix: stop take from starting the chain clock
chore(release): 0.2.0
```
